From: Emily Astranova <emily@astralabs.dev>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 00:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: hold the VFE required-opp only while the domain is on

A camss node may carry required-opps for its VFE power domains so that the
parent rail (MMCX on SM8150) is raised while a pipeline runs. On SM8150 the
600 MHz CSID clock does not come out of reset at the rail's idle corner, so
without such a vote the first stream after the display drops MMCX to low SVS
fails with "CSID reset timeout" and the graph is dead until reboot.

genpd records a required-opp performance state when the virtual power-domain
device is attached and only parks it when that device runtime-suspends. camss
drives the VFE domains through device links instead, so a domain that has not
been used yet, or that this board never uses, keeps the attach-time vote
forever and pins the parent rail at the camera corner while idle.

Cycle each VFE domain device through runtime resume and suspend once the
camss device itself has runtime PM enabled. genpd then parks the vote in
rpm_pstate, restores it when a device link activates the domain, and drops it
again when the link goes away.

Signed-off-by: Emily Astranova <emily@astralabs.dev>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -3860,6 +3860,26 @@ static int camss_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * A required-opp vote on a VFE power domain is recorded when the
+	 * domain device is attached and is only parked by a runtime suspend
+	 * of that device. The domains are driven through device links, so
+	 * give each one a resume/suspend cycle now; otherwise an unused
+	 * domain holds the vote, and with it the parent rail, forever.
+	 */
+	for (int i = 0; i < camss->res->vfe_num; i++) {
+		struct device *genpd = camss->vfe[i].genpd;
+
+		if (!genpd)
+			continue;
+
+		ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(genpd);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(dev, "vfe%d pm domain cycle failed: %d\n", i, ret);
+		else
+			pm_runtime_put_sync_suspend(genpd);
+	}
+
 	num_subdevs = camss_of_parse_ports(camss);
 	if (num_subdevs < 0) {
 		ret = num_subdevs;
